hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16047","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said, my father narrated to me, he said, Layth narrated to us, from Talhah, from his father, from his grandfather, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping his head until he reached the nape and what follows it of the front of the neck, once. He said, the nape is the side of the neck."
